cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ant Piano-Movers RL: a reinforcement-learning environment for the puzzle ants solve"
message: "If you use this environment or the write-up in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kakooee
    given-names: Reza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2946-9668"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RezaKakooee/ant-piano-movers-rl"
url: "https://rezakakooee.github.io/ant-piano-movers-rl/"
abstract: >-
  A Gymnasium environment recreating the cooperative-transport "piano-movers"
  experiment of Dreyer et al. (PNAS 2025), in which crazy ants move a T-shaped
  load through two narrow slits. The load is wider than the slit and the middle
  corridor is shorter than the load, so the task can only be solved by entering
  big-head first, turning inside the corridor, and exiting small-head first.
  This makes it a deceptive-exploration benchmark: straight-line distance
  shaping points through the walls and punishes the required turn. The repo
  includes the environment, a BFS route-distance ("geodesic") reward, a
  curriculum whose stages are taken from a real solution path, SAC and PPO
  training scripts, and a browser sandbox.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - motion planning
  - piano movers problem
  - collective behaviour
  - cooperative transport
  - gymnasium environment
